# The data each release wrote (crates/vcon-server/tests/formats.rs) is bytes:
# sealed objects, catalogs, keys and empty lock files. Git's own test for
# binary looks for a NUL byte, which some of these lack, and would then diff,
# merge and grep them as text; the commit hook's scan of staged lines would
# read their bytes as UTF-8. The manifests are JSON and stay text.
crates/vcon-server/tests/data/formats/** binary
crates/vcon-server/tests/data/formats/*/manifest.json diff merge text
